 "differences": [
  "The PhysioNet page says 20 years < age < 30 years, but Subject_info.csv lists ages 21 to 29: 0 participant(s) are at the edge of the stated range.",
  "Foot-switch values converted with the header's gain (2 per V) range from about -2000 to 30000, which cannot be volts; they are kept as the header gives them and flagged in channel_units.",
  "The v1.0.1 headers of two participants (the two replaced in that version) give the units as mV where all others say uV (sEMG), V and deg; their signal amplitude matches the others, so values are treated as uV. The paper itself (paywalled) could not be read; the published checks use the PhysioNet description, which the authors wrote for the same dataset."
